// Range requests, RFC 9110 §14 and §13.1.5:
// https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110#section-14
//
// Asking for part of something instead of all of it. This is what a download
// resumes with, what a player seeks with, and what a segment of a media stream
// is fetched with — one field asking, one field answering, and the arithmetic
// in between that turns "the last 500 bytes" into two offsets.
//
// Offsets are 64-bit. A representation larger than two gigabytes is ordinary
// for the thing range requests exist to serve, and a 32-bit offset would fail
// on exactly the files people seek within.
import {
  "moonbitstack/moonhttp/range",
} for "test"
